<* comment
   Noctalia user template. Renders the live palette for wall-in-one.

   Registered under [theme.templates.user.wall-in-one] in Noctalia's
   settings.toml by `wall-in-one --install-theme-template`. Noctalia re-renders
   this on every palette change, then runs the template's post_hook, which is
   what pushes the new colours into the running app.

   The colour loop is generic on purpose, so tokens added by a future Noctalia
   version flow through without this file needing an edit.

   Note: an unrecognised block is silently skipped by Noctalia's template
   engine, which is what makes this a comment. Do not write a block-closing
   delimiter inside it -- the engine's block regex is non-greedy and would end
   the comment there, spilling the rest into the output.
*>
{
  "mode": "{{mode}}",
  "colors": {
<* for name, value in colors *>
    "{{name}}": "{{value.default.hex}}"<* if not loop.last *>,<* endif *>
<* endfor *>
  }
}
